<main class="review-card" style="max-width: 980px">
  <%= link_to "← Conversation queue", root_path, class: "text-link" %>
  <p class="eyebrow mt-7">GOOGLE WORKSPACE CONNECTION</p>
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-2">Gmail for the inquiry desk</h1>
  <p class="muted mt-3"><%= GmailConnection::MAILBOX %> · replies from <%= GmailConnection::SALES_ADDRESS %></p>
  <div class="approved-box mt-6"><strong>Status: <%= @connection.status.humanize %></strong><p class="mt-2">Polling: <%= @connection.polling_enabled? ? "On" : "Off" %> · Live sending: <%= @connection.sending_enabled? ? "Enabled, with approval and confirmation for each reply" : "Off" %></p><p class="mt-2">Last successful sync: <%= @connection.last_synced_at&.strftime("%b %-d, %H:%M:%S") || "Not yet synchronized" %></p><% if @connection.last_error.present? %><p role="alert" class="mt-3">Connection error: <%= @connection.last_error.humanize %>. Check the setup below or reconnect.</p><% end %></div>
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-7 mb-4">1. Create the Google OAuth client</h2>
  <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 text-sm leading-7">
    <li>Sign in to <a class="text-link" href="https://console.cloud.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Cloud</a> as Kevin, create a project under the Breeze Block Workspace organization, and enable the Gmail API.</li>
    <li>In Google Auth Platform, configure Branding, set Audience to <strong>Internal</strong>, and add these two Data Access scopes: <code>gmail.readonly</code> and <code>gmail.send</code>.</li>
    <li>Create a <strong>Web application</strong> OAuth client. Register this exact authorized redirect URI:<br><code class="break-all"><%= Gmail::Oauth.redirect_uri %></code></li>
    <li>Enter the client ID and client secret below. They belong only in this private app; do not paste them into chat, commit them, or put them in log files.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="muted text-xs mt-3">Use this app at the same 127.0.0.1 origin as the callback. If Google only offers External audience, check that the project belongs to your Workspace organization. Drafts remain in Rails; no mailbox modification, deletion or settings-management permissions are requested.</p>
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-7 mb-4">2. Save configuration and connect</h2>
  <%= form_with model: @connection, url: gmail_connection_path do |form| %>
    <div class="field"><%= form.label :client_id, "Google OAuth client ID" %><%= form.text_field :client_id, autocomplete: "off" %></div>
    <div class="field"><%= form.label :client_secret, "Client secret (blank keeps the saved secret)" %><%= form.password_field :client_secret, value: nil, autocomplete: "new-password" %></div>
    <div class="field"><%= form.label :shopify_senders, "Shopify contact-form notification sender addresses (comma-separated)" %><%= form.text_field :shopify_senders %><p class="muted text-xs mt-2">Check the actual notification sender in Gmail. Forms require a recognizable contact-form subject and Name / Email / Body fields. Ambiguous forms enter review rather than guessing the customer.</p></div>
    <div class="field"><%= form.label :import_since, "Import sales messages since" %><%= form.date_field :import_since, required: true %></div>
    <div class="field"><%= form.label :poll_interval_seconds, "Polling interval in seconds" %><%= form.number_field :poll_interval_seconds, min: 30, max: 3600, required: true %></div>
    <%= form.submit "Save Gmail configuration", class: "btn secondary" %>
  <% end %>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-4"><%= button_to "Connect / reconnect Google", connect_gmail_connection_path, class: "btn primary", data: { turbo: false } %><% if @connection.authorized? %><%= button_to "Sync now", sync_gmail_connection_path, class: "btn secondary" %><%= button_to "Disconnect Gmail", disconnect_gmail_connection_path, class: "btn secondary" %><% end %></div>
  <p class="muted text-xs mt-3">Authorize <%= GmailConnection::MAILBOX %>. Connecting enables read-only sales synchronization. It does not enable sending. Unrelated message bodies are not fetched or stored. Closing this page does not stop the worker.</p>
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-7 mb-4">3. Verify the sales identity</h2>
  <p class="text-sm leading-7">In Gmail → Settings → Accounts → Send mail as, confirm that <strong>sales@breezeblock.ca</strong> is accepted. Configure it in Gmail if needed. The app checks the alias through read-only API access.</p>
  <% if @connection.authorized? %>
    <% if @connection.sending_enabled? %><%= button_to "Disable live sending", disable_sending_gmail_connection_path, class: "btn secondary mt-4" %><% else %>
      <%= form_with url: enable_sending_gmail_connection_path, class: "mt-4" do |form| %><label class="flex gap-3 items-start text-sm"><%= check_box_tag :alias_confirmed, "1", false, required: true, style: "width:auto" %><span>I checked Gmail and confirmed the sales alias is an accepted Send mail as identity.</span></label><%= form.submit "Verify alias and enable reviewed sending", class: "btn primary mt-4" %><% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
  <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-7 mb-4">Messages needing import review</h2>
  <p class="muted text-xs mb-4">Only provider IDs and a fixed reason are stored here. Open the message in Gmail first. Importing is separate from sending.</p>
  <% @reviews.each do |item| %>
    <article class="message mb-4"><p class="text-sm"><%= item.reason.humanize %></p><%= link_to "Inspect this thread in Gmail", "https://mail.google.com/mail/u/?authuser=#{ERB::Util.url_encode(GmailConnection::MAILBOX)}#all/#{ERB::Util.url_encode(item.thread_id)}", class: "text-link mt-3 inline-block", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener noreferrer" %>
      <%= form_with url: gmail_review_item_path(item), method: :patch, class: "mt-4" do |form| %><div class="field"><%= label_tag "review_name_#{item.id}", "Confirmed customer name" %><%= text_field_tag :customer_name, nil, id: "review_name_#{item.id}" %></div><div class="field"><%= label_tag "review_email_#{item.id}", "Confirmed customer email" %><%= email_field_tag :customer_email, nil, id: "review_email_#{item.id}", required: true %></div><label class="flex gap-3 text-sm"><%= check_box_tag :confirm_import, "1", false, required: true, style: "width:auto" %><span>I checked Gmail and confirm this is a sales inquiry for this customer.</span></label><%= form.submit "Import selected sales inquiry", class: "btn secondary mt-3" %><% end %>
      <%= button_to "Dismiss without importing", gmail_review_item_path(item), method: :patch, params: { dismiss: "1" }, class: "text-link mt-3" %>
    </article>
  <% end %>
  <% if @reviews.empty? %><p class="muted text-sm">No messages awaiting import review.</p><% end %>
</main>
